  <exercise xml:id="ex-riemann-sum-limit-to-integral">
    <provenance>
      <dc:creator>Claude</dc:creator>
      <ns1:created>2026-08-22</ns1:created>
    </provenance>
    <introduction>
      <p>
        The limit
        <md>
          \lim_{n \to \infty} \sum_{i=1}^n \left(1 + \frac{3i}{n}\right)\frac{3}{n}
        </md>
        is the limit of a right Riemann sum for a definite integral <m>\int_a^b f(x)\,dx</m> of some function <m>f</m> over some interval <m>[a,b]</m>.
      </p>
    </introduction>

    <task>
      <statement>
        <p>
          Identify <m>a</m>, <m>b</m>, and <m>f(x)</m>, and write the corresponding definite integral.
        </p>
      </statement>

      </task>

    <task>
      <statement>
        <p>
          Evaluate the integral using the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus.
        </p>
      </statement>

      </task>
  </exercise>

